The scattered changes adding the "xpress" method can probably be minimized if you dispatch under method="dflash" the same way dflash2 does. The inheritance structure already reflects this: `class XPressSpeculator(DFlashSpeculator)`. Something along the lines of:
```python
elif speculative_config.method == "dflash":
    architectures = speculative_config.draft_model_config.architectures
    if "Qwen3XPressModel" in architectures:
        return XPressSpeculator(vllm_config, device)
    if "DFlash2DraftModel" in architectures:
        return DFlash2Speculator(vllm_config, device)
```
